## 1. The Buyer Will Open a Dispute (Appeal)
When the buyer transfers the XAF to your MTN MoMo, they will click "Transferred, notify seller." If you do not release the crypto within the designated countdown timer (usually 15 to 30 minutes), the buyer will click "Appeal" or "Dispute."

* The platform will lock your crypto asset securely in escrow.
* The buyer will upload their MTN MoMo transaction receipt or transaction ID as proof that they paid you.

## 2. Your Account Is At Risk of Being Banned
P2P platforms take holding funds hostage very seriously. If you receive the XAF and ignore the order:

* The platform’s customer support will send you urgent notifications via app, SMS, or email giving you a short window (often 2 to 6 hours) to respond.
* If you fail to respond or refuse to release the crypto, the platform will manually force-release your crypto to the buyer.
* Your account will likely be permanently banned or restricted for malicious behavior/bad faith trading.

## 3. What You Should Do Right Now
If you realize you just made this mistake, fix it immediately to protect your account standing:

* Check the Order History: Log into your trading app (Binance, NoOnes, Bybit, etc.), go to your P2P orders, and look under the "Pending" or "Appeal" tabs.
* Verify Your Balance: Double-check your MoMo balance (*126#) to confirm the exact XAF amount is still safely there.
* Release the Crypto: If the order is still open or in appeal, simply click the "Payment Received" or "Release Crypto" button. This closes the dispute instantly and amicably.
* Talk to the Buyer: Drop a quick message in the P2P order chat box saying, "Sorry for the delay, I just checked my balance and released the crypto now."

